{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"becoming-entire-morayeel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nBug dbe8-cf03-ed53-47e7 fixed autodeploy.sh so a comment-only edit to a watched Gerrit config file does not emit AUTODEPLOY_ERROR config_manual (Gerrit change 3095, commit 67137e66e99). Tests cover it with a stubbed git; no live commit has exercised it on the host yet.\n\n## Approach\nWait for the next commit that edits only comments or whitespace in a path in CONFIG_PATHS (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh), then read the host journal for the deploy of that commit. If no such commit lands within a reasonable time, close as not observable.\n\n## Testing\nRead-only: journalctl -u rebar-autodeploy.service on the Gerrit host for the deploy window of that commit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The journal for the deploy of a comment-only config commit contains no config_manual AUTODEPLOY_ERROR (checked: journalctl output recorded in a ticket comment with the commit sha).\n","id":"01b8-d3aa-2c48-4e5d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["autodeploy","ops","verification"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Confirm a live comment-only config commit no longer emits config_manual"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792820482239307001,"uuid":"3f1436ab-b2fb-43b0-8bd1-0ee76face10d"}